+Program-generation checks (apply before returning the first program and every revision):
+There are only 3 model sessions, 2 Blender executions and 600 seconds. Check the entire
+program against the API before spending an execution; after an error, audit subsequent
+code too, since the traceback stops at the first failure. Return a complete corrected
+program when an execution remains. An unexecuted revision is not a successful build.
+If execution fails without a render, diagnose the traceback; visual quality and editability
+remain unknown. Do not infer a visual discrepancy or claim success from missing output.
+
+All primitive dimensions and radii must be finite and strictly positive. For every
+fillet_box, including cutters and helper-generated instances, require
+0 < radius <= min(size)/2 across ALL THREE dimensions, including thickness. Prefer a
+strict margin below this limit. fillet_box rounds in 3D; it is not a planar rounded
+rectangle with an independent extrusion thickness. For thin parts use a box when rounding
+is unimportant, or construct a valid thicker rounded shape and resize it about its center
+to the desired thickness. Do not enlarge the final part merely to satisfy the radius.
+Rod endpoints and consecutive sweep_tube points must be distinct.
+
+realize(scene) clears Blender with factory settings. Any previous Blender world, camera,
+lights or materials must not be assumed to survive. Configure them after realize.
+In particular, bpy.context.scene.world may be None. If configuring world nodes, initialize
+and assign a world first, using this pattern after realize:
+    world = bpy.context.scene.world
+    if world is None:
+        world = bpy.data.worlds.new('SceneWorld')
+        bpy.context.scene.world = world
+    world.use_nodes = True
+    background = world.node_tree.nodes.get('Background')
+    if background is None:
+        background = world.node_tree.nodes.new('ShaderNodeBackground')
+    output = world.node_tree.nodes.get('World Output')
+    if output is None:
+        output = world.node_tree.nodes.new('ShaderNodeOutputWorld')
+    world.node_tree.links.new(background.outputs['Background'], output.inputs['Surface'])
